# Rank 1177 / CVE-2026-27700: Hono's AWS Lambda adapter falls back to
# X-Forwarded-For for ALB events, reading the header's first comma-separated
# entry as the client address (CWE-290, CWE-345):
#
#   const xff = c.req.header('x-forwarded-for')
#   if (xff) {
#     address = xff.split(',')[0].trim()
#   }
#
# ALB appends the connection's real peer IP to the end of the header, so the
# leading entries are whatever the client sent. A request carrying
# `X-Forwarded-For: 10.0.0.1, <attacker-ip>` reads back as address
# "10.0.0.1", spoofing past ipRestriction middleware built on getConnInfo's
# result. The fixed revision reads the last entry instead, the one ALB
# itself appends.
#
# FIXED. javascript.flags binds proxyClientIpSpoofingBypass904 in
# mfb63017a.vyql: a function-scoped presence match on a `req.header(...)`
# call naming "x-forwarded-for", a subscript keyed [0] on that call's `split`
# result, and the split result assigned into something named "address". The
# subscript key ties the match to the specific first-element read rather than
# any array index in the function, and the "address" name follows Node's own
# `socket.remoteAddress` convention that connection-info helpers across
# Express, Fastify and Hono repeat, so the binding is answerable to that
# convention rather than to this adapter's internals. It reuses
# code.ProxyClientIpSpoofingBypass (VYQL-AUTH-012), shipped for rank330's
# CasaOS gateway-forwarding case: same weakness -- a spoofable client-IP
# header trusted for an access-control decision -- read out of a
# header-parsing helper instead of a proxy hop. Selecting the header's last
# entry (the fixed form) or any other subscript key does not match.
#
# Measured against both revisions and both directions below. Full spec
# suite green. OWASP Java +1.00 and Python +0.90, unchanged (javascript-only
# change, no other language's bindings touched).

test "rank1177: ALB conn-info reads the first X-Forwarded-For entry as the client address"
  lang javascript
  file src/adapter/aws-lambda/conninfo.ts
  expect VYQL-AUTH-012
  expect_review code.ProxyClientIpSpoofingBypass
  code
  ```
  export const getConnInfo = (c) => {
    let address

    if ('identity' in c.env.requestContext && c.env.requestContext.identity?.sourceIp) {
      address = c.env.requestContext.identity.sourceIp
    } else {
      const xff = c.req.header('x-forwarded-for')
      if (xff) {
        // First IP is the client
        address = xff.split(',')[0].trim()
      }
    }

    return {
      remote: {
        address,
      },
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1177: ALB conn-info reads the last X-Forwarded-For entry, the one ALB appended"
  lang javascript
  file src/adapter/aws-lambda/conninfo.ts
  reject VYQL-AUTH-012
  reject_review code.ProxyClientIpSpoofingBypass
  code
  ```
  export const getConnInfo = (c) => {
    let address

    if ('identity' in c.env.requestContext && c.env.requestContext.identity?.sourceIp) {
      address = c.env.requestContext.identity.sourceIp
    } else {
      const xff = c.req.header('x-forwarded-for')
      if (xff) {
        const ips = xff.split(',')
        // ALB appends the real client IP to the end of the header
        address = ips[ips.length - 1].trim()
      }
    }

    return {
      remote: {
        address,
      },
    }
  }
  ```
